
# Assignment 4.1 — Student Registration Form

## 1. Objective

To create a student registration form using HTML. The form includes Full Name, Email, Password, Phone Number, Age, and a Submit button. Proper labels, input types, unique IDs, meaningful names, and required attributes are used.

## 2. HTML Code (registration.html)

Create a file named `registration.html` and add the following code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Student Registration Form</title>
</head>
<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Student Registration Form</h1>
        <p>Please fill in the details below to register.</p>
    </header>

    <hr>

    <main>
        <form action="#" method="post">

            <div>
                <label for="fullName">Full Name:</label>
                <input
                    type="text"
                    id="fullName"
                    name="fullName"
                    placeholder="Enter your full name"
                    required>
            </div>

            <br>

            <div>
                <label for="email">Email Address:</label>
                <input
                    type="email"
                    id="email"
                    name="email"
                    placeholder="Enter your email address"
                    required>
            </div>

            <br>

            <div>
                <label for="password">Password:</label>
                <input
                    type="password"
                    id="password"
                    name="password"
                    placeholder="Create a password"
                    minlength="8"
                    required>
            </div>

            <br>

            <div>
                <label for="phone">Phone Number:</label>
                <input
                    type="tel"
                    id="phone"
                    name="phone"
                    placeholder="Enter your phone number"
                    pattern="[0-9]{10}"
                    title="Please enter a 10-digit phone number"
                    required>
            </div>

            <br>

            <div>
                <label for="age">Age:</label>
                <input
                    type="number"
                    id="age"
                    name="age"
                    placeholder="Enter your age"
                    min="1"
                    max="120"
                    required>
            </div>

            <br>

            <button type="submit">Register</button>

        </form>
    </main>

    <hr>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2026 Student Registration Form</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
```

## 3. Explanation of HTML Elements

1. `<form>`: Defines the student registration form.
2. `<label>`: Provides a descriptive label for each input field.
3. `type="text"`: Accepts the student's full name.
4. `type="email"`: Accepts an email address and checks its basic format.
5. `type="password"`: Hides the characters entered in the password field.
6. `type="tel"`: Accepts a phone number.
7. `type="number"`: Accepts a numeric age value.
8. `id`: Gives each input a unique identifier.
9. `name`: Identifies the field when form data is submitted.
10. `required`: Prevents submission when a mandatory field is empty.
11. `minlength="8"`: Requires a password with at least eight characters.
12. `pattern="[0-9]{10}"`: Requires exactly 10 digits in the phone number field.
13. `<button type="submit">`: Creates the Register button.

## 4. How to Run the Project

1. Open Visual Studio Code.
2. Create a folder named `student-registration`.
3. Create a file named `registration.html`.
4. Copy the HTML code into the file.
5. Save the file.
6. Open `registration.html` in a web browser or use the Live Server extension.
7. Enter sample details in all the fields.
8. Click the Register button to test the form.
9. Leave a required field empty to verify that the browser displays a validation message.
10. Take a screenshot of the working form for submission.

## 5. Expected Result

The webpage will display:

- A Student Registration Form heading.
- A Full Name input field.
- An Email Address input field.
- A Password input field.
- A Phone Number input field.
- An Age input field.
- A Register button.
- A footer with copyright information.

The browser will validate required fields, email format, password length, phone number format, and age range.

## 6. Important Note

This assignment creates the front-end form only. The `action="#"` attribute does not store registration details in a database or send them to a server. A backend is required to process and store actual student registrations. Do not use real passwords when testing this sample form.

